---
---
<figure class="flow">
  <svg class="dsk" viewBox="0 0 960 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-t flow-d" focusable="false">
    <title id="flow-t">How Albena works</title>
    <desc id="flow-d">You speak to Albena. Your voice is processed on hardware you own, a Mac or an NVIDIA machine. That hardware talks to your home, media, work and optional cloud services. A privacy lane runs under everything: nothing leaves your house unless you allow it.</desc>
    <defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" fill="#a5a8ff"/></marker></defs>
    <g class="n">
      <rect x="20" y="70" width="190" height="130" rx="16"/>
      <text x="115" y="112" class="h">1. You speak</text>
      <text x="115" y="140" class="s">&ldquo;Hey Albena&rdquo;</text>
      <text x="115" y="164" class="s">voice or text</text>
    </g>
    <g class="n hw">
      <rect x="365" y="40" width="230" height="190" rx="16"/>
      <text x="480" y="82" class="h">2. Your hardware</text>
      <text x="480" y="112" class="s">Mac or NVIDIA box</text>
      <text x="480" y="136" class="s">Local models</text>
      <text x="480" y="160" class="s">Memory you can erase</text>
      <text x="480" y="184" class="s">Approval gate</text>
    </g>
    <g class="n">
      <rect x="750" y="20" width="190" height="62" rx="14"/><text x="845" y="57" class="h2">Home devices</text>
      <rect x="750" y="94" width="190" height="62" rx="14"/><text x="845" y="131" class="h2">Media &amp; work tools</text>
      <rect x="750" y="168" width="190" height="62" rx="14"/><text x="845" y="205" class="h2">Your own systems</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M210 135H365" class="ar"/><path d="M595 135H750" class="ar"/>
    <text x="298" y="124" class="t">on-device</text><text x="662" y="124" class="t">asks first</text>
    <g class="opt">
      <rect x="750" y="250" width="190" height="50" rx="14"/><text x="845" y="280" class="h2">Optional cloud</text>
      <path d="M595 200 L750 275" class="ar dash"/>
    </g>
    <g class="lane">
      <rect x="20" y="318" width="920" height="34" rx="17"/>
      <text x="480" y="340" class="lt">Privacy lane: nothing leaves your house unless you allow it</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <svg class="mob" viewBox="0 0 340 600" role="img" aria-labelledby="flowm-t" focusable="false">
    <title id="flowm-t">How Albena works: you speak, your hardware handles it locally, then it reaches your home and systems after asking. Optional cloud is off by default. Nothing leaves your house unless you allow it.</title>
    <defs><marker id="ahm" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" fill="#a5a8ff"/></marker></defs>
    <g class="n"><rect x="40" y="10" width="260" height="70" rx="14"/><text x="170" y="40" class="h">1. You speak</text><text x="170" y="66" class="s">&ldquo;Hey Albena&rdquo;, voice or text</text></g>
    <path d="M170 82V120" class="ar m"/>
    <g class="n hw"><rect x="40" y="124" width="260" height="130" rx="14"/><text x="170" y="154" class="h">2. Your hardware</text><text x="170" y="182" class="s">Mac or NVIDIA box</text><text x="170" y="206" class="s">Local models and memory</text><text x="170" y="230" class="s">Approval gate</text></g>
    <path d="M170 256V294" class="ar m"/><text x="180" y="280" class="t" style="text-anchor:start">asks first</text>
    <g class="n"><rect x="40" y="298" width="260" height="130" rx="14"/><text x="170" y="328" class="h">3. Your home and systems</text><text x="170" y="360" class="s">Home devices</text><text x="170" y="384" class="s">Media and work tools</text><text x="170" y="408" class="s">Your own systems</text></g>
    <g class="opt"><rect x="40" y="446" width="260" height="46" rx="14"/><text x="170" y="474" class="s">Cloud model (optional, off)</text></g>
    <g class="lane"><rect x="10" y="516" width="320" height="64" rx="16"/><text x="170" y="542" class="lt">Privacy lane</text><text x="170" y="566" class="lt">Nothing leaves unless you allow it</text></g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Everyday requests stay inside the house. The dashed path is optional and off unless you turn it on.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .flow { margin: 0; }
  .flow svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; min-width: 0; }
  .n rect { fill: #121316; stroke: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .hw rect { stroke: #a5a8ff; fill: #16172a; }
  text { text-anchor: middle; fill: #d0d6e0; font-family: Inter Variable, Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .h { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 600; fill: #f7f8f8; }
  .h2 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; fill: #f7f8f8; }
  .s { font-size: 16px; }
  .t { font-size: 14px; fill: #d0d6e0; }
  .flow svg.mob { display: none; }
  .ar.m { marker-end: url(#ahm); }
  .ar { fill: none; stroke: #a5a8ff; stroke-width: 2.4; marker-end: url(#ah); }
  .dash { stroke-dasharray: 6 6; stroke: #f2c94c; }
  .opt rect { fill: #121316; stroke: #f2c94c; stroke-dasharray: 6 5; stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .lane rect { fill: rgba(76, 183, 130, 0.14); stroke: #4cb782; stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .lt { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; fill: #9be8c0; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--fg-2); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .flow svg.dsk { display: none; } .flow svg.mob { display: block; max-width: 420px; margin: 0 auto; } .mob .h { font-size: 19px; } .mob .s { font-size: 15.5px; } .mob .t { font-size: 15px; } .mob .lt { font-size: 15.5px; } }
</style>
